# ===========================================================================
# Hospital Management System (HMS) - Frontend Docker build-context ignore file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The compose `frontend` service sets `build.context: ./frontend`, so this
# file lives at the build-context root and IS honored by the Docker builder.
# Every pattern below is EXCLUDED from the context sent to the daemon.
#
# Goals:
#   * Keep the image small and the build fast (smaller context = faster COPY).
#   * NEVER leak the host's node_modules (may contain platform-specific native
#     binaries) - the Dockerfile runs a fresh `npm ci` / `npm install` inside
#     the image, so host dependencies must not be copied in.
#   * NEVER leak local secrets (.env) into the image layers.
#
# Syntax: plain text, one glob per line; lines starting with `#` are comments;
# a leading `!` re-includes an otherwise-ignored path.
#
# Do NOT add build inputs here (package.json, package-lock.json, index.html,
# vite.config.js, nginx.conf, public/, src/) - they are required to build.
# ===========================================================================

# dependencies
node_modules

# build output
dist
build
coverage

# env & secrets
.env
.env.*
# keep the committed, non-secret template available to the build context
!.env.example

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# vcs & editor
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# docker
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# tests & tooling that need not be in the image
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.jsx
**/__tests__
.eslintcache
